From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:35:30 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-tegu: Give the main PMIC
 its interrupt

Without an interrupt the S2MPG14 driver supplies its rails but none of
the PMIC's events reach the host ("no interrupt, so no RTC alarm" at
boot), so rtc0 has no wake alarm: on the Pixel 9a a suspend with an RTC
alarm armed slept until a key was pressed (2026-11-09, on the published
tree). The interrupt is GIC SPI 74, latched by the VGPIO2AP sysreg, as
the gs201 boards' nodes have it; wakeup-source makes the alarm a wake
source, the first one for suspend.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
index 5e7eb363f..764142419 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
@@ -202,6 +202,9 @@ &acpm_ipc {
 
 	pmic-1 {
 		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg14-pmic";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 74 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		google,vgpio2ap-sysreg = <&sysreg_vgpio2ap>;
+		wakeup-source;
 
 		regulators {
 			touch_avdd: ldo4m {
